{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ig6kiecsawjqsjn6rncexitv6i4y3ah2ubsnl77x4bbblparhnia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four phases complete. Phase D gate verified.\n\n## Results\n\n**Phase A** — Both build clean. C: `cmake -S c_src -B <dir> && cmake --build <dir>` → `driver`. Rust: `cargo build --release` (compiled with no errors on first try, no warnings).\n\n**Phase B/C** — `translation/tests/differential.rs`: 20 tests driving both binaries as subprocesses, comparing stdout, stderr, and exit status (including death-by-signal). Plus an independent byte-exact sweep of **465 inputs, 0 mismatches**.\n\n### Three real bugs found and fixed\n\nThe happy path passed immediately — all 32 initial cases matched. The bugs were all in output/signal handling, and only surfaced once I probed *how the program dies*:\n\n**1. `print!` panicked where C's `printf` fails silently.** With stdout on a reader-less pipe and SIGPIPE inherited as `SIG_IGN`: C exited 0 silently; Rust aborted with SIGABRT plus `failed printing to stdout: Broken pipe` on stderr. `panic = \"abort\"` turned the panic into a wrong exit status *and* extra stderr bytes. Fixed by `write_all` with the result discarded, as C discards `printf`'s return value.\n\n**2. Rust's runtime forced `SIGPIPE = SIG_IGN` before `main`.** With SIGPIPE at `SIG_DFL`, C dies with signal 13; Rust exited 0. Hard-coding `signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_DFL)` would have been wrong too — it breaks case 1. Fixed with a `.init_array` constructor that runs *before* `std::rt::init`, captures the inherited disposition, and restores it in `main`. Both dispositions now match.\n\n> This was easy to miss because the harness itself had SIGPIPE ignored, so the C behavior to replicate was environment-dependent. That's why I tested both dispositions explicitly.\n\n**3. `read_to_end` blocked where C didn't.** Given `\"7 2 \"` on a pipe left open, C printed and exited; Rust hung forever. `scanf` pulls from a buffered `FILE*` and stops as soon as the second `%d` terminates. Fixed with a lazily-filled 4096-byte (`BUFSIZ`) buffer. This also preserves the converse: for `\"7 2\"` with no terminating byte, **C itself blocks** waiting for one more character — and the translation now blocks identically (asserted in `blocks_exactly_where_c_blocks`).\n\n### Verified already-correct (highest-risk areas)\n- `div(x,0)` and `div(INT_MIN,-1)` are UB; the translation uses inline `cdq; idiv` so it dies by SIGFPE with empty stdout, rather than a Rust panic (which would give SIGABRT + stderr text).\n- glibc's `%d` converts through a `long`, saturating at `LONG_MAX`/`LONG_MIN` then truncating — so `\"99999999999999999999999\"` → `-1` and `\"4294967296\"` → `0`.\n- Untouched variables keep their `1` initialiser on matching/input failure.\n\nI also confirmed the two randomized sweeps aren't degenerate (388 distinct inputs; 28 of the 250 integer pairs hit a faulting divisor) — a seeded RNG can silently generate near-identical cases and look like coverage.\n\n**Gate:** both build clean · 20/20 pass in debug *and* release · 0 ignored/skipped · `c_src/` md5sums unchanged (the harness builds CMake into `target/c_reference_build/`, never writing into the C tree) · no `no_mangle`/`cdylib`/`libloading`. Findings recorded in `translation/ERRORS.md`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2832,"cache_read_input_tokens":83878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2832,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02bcd690-ac6a-413d-9a7f-7ee18a5188e0","uuid":"737ccc6b-43af-4e3d-bbe4-a63c60bdd126","timestamp":"2026-08-28T13:51:49.618Z"}
